139    /** FUNCTION otap_api.finish_test_with_exit_code
140    * This function is for automation purposes. It translates and returns an exit code that can be uses in CMD and shell scripts
141    * to handle reactions based on the output of a test session, e.g. if test is passed you don't need probably the test report. Or you want
142    * your build to fail, if test is not passed.
143    *
144    * Equal to finish_test apart from the return value check and translation. Undefined overrules failed. If undefined is returned, also
145    * failed tests may be contained in the current test report. If you finish a test session without any test run, the result is UNDEFINED.
146    *
147    * @param p_write_count_rec The indicator, if record count test should be done and written. Either otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TRUE or otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_FALSE.
148    * @param o_otap_session The current session_record from OTAP_TEST package.
149    *
150    * @return A positive integer as result. 0 = success, all tests passed. 1 = at least one test failed. 2 = at least one test undefined.
151    *
152    * @exception -20099 Internal error, invalid OTAP_SESSION object.
153    */
154    FUNCTION finish_test_with_exit_code( p_write_count_rec IN	    NUMBER
155  					  , o_otap_session    IN OUT NOCOPY OTAP_SESSION
