109    /** FUNCTION otap_logic.throws_ok
110    * Checks if a given statement or code block throws the expected error message. The expected error message must match
111    * the SQLERRM returned from exception thrown. Use throws_match or throws_like if only parts of the error message must
112    * match. If the statement starts with SELECT it is executed as is, without caring for returned columns or rows and ignoring
113    * any given header definition. The header definition is a code block for the declare section defining variables that may be
114    * needed by called functions or procedures. It is only used if the statement does not start with SELECT and if the declaration
115    * block can be executed with a NULL procedure without throwing exceptions.
116    *
117    * Function comes in two flavors, comparing SQLERRM as VARCHAR2 or the error code SQLCODE as number. It can also be used to check
118    * if a statement does not cause any exception by switching the expected result to otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TEST_FAILED.
119    *
120    * SQL statements (SELECT, UPDATE, DELETE) MUST NOT have a trailing semicolon. otap will try to detect and remove it, but may fail.
121    * Semicolon in dynamically executed SQL statements will cause an unexpected exception.
122    *
123    * Functions and procedures MUST have a trailing semicolon, especially if more than one command is executed in the block.
124    *
125    * Syntax errors will most likely cause a different exception as the expected one and fail the test. This is especially important if
126    * you switch the expected test result. otap expects in this case, that the statement could be executed without any exception.
127    *
128    * @param p_statement Mandatory. The statement as string to execute. Can be a select statement or function/procedure call. No need to proovide a begin end block. Syntax should be checked or will cause unexpected exceptions.
129    * @param p_sqlerrm Mandatory. The exact case sensitive expected error message as returned by SQLERRM after a provoked exception.
130    * @param o_error Error information, if any, on the test executed.
131    * @param p_header_def Optional valid header definition (test result is undefined if header is not valid) for function or procedure tests to support OUT and return variables.
132    * @param p_expected_result The expected test result as number. Default is test passed. See otap_constants.
133    *
134    * @return The test result as number, either otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TEST_PASSED, otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TEST_FAILED or otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TEST_UNDEFINED.
135    */
136    FUNCTION throws_ok( p_statement	     IN 	   VARCHAR2
137  			 , p_sqlerrm	     IN 	   VARCHAR2
138  			 , o_errors		OUT NOCOPY VARCHAR2
139  			 , p_header_def      IN 	   VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
140  			 , p_expected_result IN 	   NUMBER   DEFAULT otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TEST_PASSED
141  			 )
142  	 RETURN INTEGER
143    ;
