112    /** FUNCTION otap_test.finish_test_with_exit_code
113    * This function is for automation purposes. It translates and returns an exit code that can be uses in CMD and shell scripts
114    * to handle reactions based on the output of a test session, e.g. if test is passed you don't need probably the test report. Or you want
115    * your build to fail, if test is not passed.
116    *
117    * Equal to finish_test apart from the return value check and translation. Undefined overrules failed. If undefined is returned, also
118    * failed tests may be contained in the current test report. If you finish a test session without any test run, the result is UNDEFINED.
119    *
120    * @param p_write_count_rec The indicator, if record count test should be done and written. Either otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TRUE or otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_FALSE.
121    *
122    * @return A positive integer as result. 0 = success, all tests passed. 1 = at least one test failed. 2 = at least one test undefined.
123    *
124    * @exception -20099 Internal error, invalid OTAP_SESSION object.
