287    /** FUNCTION otap_test.has_column
288    * Tests if a table column exists. Additional tests on the column can be added by using the additional
289    * parameters with default NULL. The expected values have to match the content of DBA_TAB_COLUMNS for the given table,
290    * column and schema.
291    *
292    * If checking defaults, it is limited to defaults not longer than 4000 char, using the DATA_DEFAULT_VC column. Expressions
293    * must match all chars in the default, like quotation. Use q-syntax where possible to define correct strings, e.g.
294    * SELECT q'[SYS_CONTEXT('USERENV', 'OS_USER')]' FROM dual;
295    *
296    * @param p_table_name The name of the table, taken as is. Case sensitive.
297    * @param p_column_name The column name of the table, taken as is. Case sensitive.
298    * @param p_schema A schema override of the current test session if needed, taken as is. If given the table and column must exist in this schema. Case sensitive.
299    * @param p_description The test description if any. If not given, a description is generated, see template.
300    * @param p_data_type Optional check the datatype of the column. Ignored if NULL. NOT case sensitive.
301    * @param p_data_length Optional check the data length of the column. Ignored if NULL.
302    * @param p_data_precision Optional check the data precision of the column. Ignored if NULL. Results in test error if datatype is not NUMBER.
303    * @param p_data_scale Optional check the data scale of the column. Ignored if NULL. Results in test error if datatype is not NUMBER or TIMESTAMP.
304    * @param p_nullable Optional check if the column is nullable. Ignored if NULL. NOT case sensitive.
305    * @param p_data_default Optional check the default for the column. Ignored if NULL. Must match all chars, including ' and ". Limited to defaults shorter than 4000 chars.
306    * @param p_expected_result The expected test result, 1 (Passed), -1 (FAILED), 0 (UNDEFINED). Default is 1 (Passed).
307    *
308    * @return The test result as text.
309    */
