484    /** FUNCTION otap_test.has_not_null_constraint
485    * Checks if a given table column has a not null check constraint. Optional you can specify the constraint name. NOT NULL constraint is
486    * somewhat special as it is recommended for inline creation, which generates system constraint names. You are also free to create it
487    * outbound. Therefore in most cases the constraint name is not defined or may change on recreation. Also NULLABLE may not reflect an
488    * existing outbound NOT NULL constraint. This function checks also the definition, which has the generated format: "COLUMN_NAME" IS NOT NULL.
489    * Any outbund declaration will probably look different. Therefore the term "IS NOT NULL" and the column name is searched after UPPER conversion
490    * of SEARCH_CONDITION_VC. Will not work for search conditions > 4000 char.
491    *
492    * @param p_table_name Mandatory. The table to be checked for NOT NULL constraint, take as is. Case sensitive. Missing value will cause test to fail.
493    * @param p_column_name Mandator. The column that is checked for the NOT NULL constraint. Case sensitive.
494    * @param p_constraint Optional. The name of the constraint. Case sensitive.
495    * @param p_schema A schema override of the current test session if needed, taken as is. If given the table and constraint must exist in this schema. Case sensitive.
496    * @param p_description The test description if any. If not given, a description is generated, see template.
497    * @param p_expected_result The expected test result as number. Default is test passed. See otap_constants.
498    *
499    * @return The test result as text.
500    */
501    FUNCTION has_not_null_constraint( p_table_name	   IN VARCHAR2
502  				       , p_column_name	   IN VARCHAR2
503  				       , p_constraint	   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
504  				       , p_schema	   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT SYS_CONTEXT('USERENV', 'CURRENT_SCHEMA')
505  				       , p_description	   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
506  				       , p_expected_result IN NUMBER   DEFAULT otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TEST_PASSED
507  				       )
508  	 RETURN VARCHAR2
509    ;
