985    /** FUNCTION otap_test.generate_schema_tests
986    * Generates the test scripts for the current available otap schema functions using by default the current
987    * schema. Test set gets defined as schema, group represents the object types, like tables, triggers and so on.
988    * No translation provided. Limited to line size 4000 but not to rows, like DBMS_OUTPUT. It is up to you how you
989    * spool the content to files.
990    *
991    * Including system generated objects is a good idea if your system is stable and you want to ensure that no one
992    * changed the current state. With CI/CD or during development, when objects get recreated, it is a really bad idea.
993    * Excluded by default are objects beginning with SYS_ for system generated object or containing $ or # chars, which
994    * may occur anywhere in the name of system objects.
995    *
996    * There is no best option, some constraints like NOT NULL must be defined inline to count a column as NOT NULL.
997    * With an additional added constraint, the column will be still marked as NULLABLE. Identity columns are another
998    * issue, as you cannot define a name for the generated sequence. Make extra tests limited on the system generated
999    * objects you rely on (like NOT NULL and identity).
1000  	*
1001  	* @param p_like_schema The LIKE expression for schema names. Default is current schema. % will generate for all schemas in the database, be careful. Underlying objects are not limited. Case sensitive.
1002  	* @param p_required_user An optional comma separated list of users required to be checked by the schema test. Will not include the selected schemas. Useful for specific schemas and integration tests.
1003  	* @param p_title_prefix An optional title prefix for set, group and test names. Limited to 10 chars. Will be added without delimiter to the processed schema.
1004  	* @param p_show_header Used to surpress header comments, init, count and finish section. Default 1 will contain all sections, otherwise skipped.
1005  	* @param p_excl_sysgen Used to ignore system generated objects identified by SYS_, # or $. Default 1 will ignore system generated objects, otherwise included.
1006  	*
1007  	* @return An OTAP_VIEW_RESULT_REC object as table type OTAP_VIEW_RESULT_TBL.
1008  	*/
1009  	FUNCTION generate_schema_tests( p_like_schema	IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT SYS_CONTEXT('USERENV', 'CURRENT_SCHEMA')
1010  				      , p_required_user IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
1011  				      , p_title_prefix	IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
1012  				      , p_show_header	IN INTEGER  DEFAULT otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TRUE
1013  				      , p_excl_sysgen	IN INTEGER  DEFAULT otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TRUE
1014  				      )
1015  	  RETURN otap_view_result_tbl PIPELINED
1016  	;
1017  
